WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.080 --> 00:00:05.040 line:10%
Ever wonder why your cells have a negative electrical charge?

2
00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:08.000 line:10%
Let's dive inside and look at the membrane.

3
00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:11.255 line:10%
First, the sodium potassium pump ...

4
00:00:11.255 --> 00:00:16.079 line:10%
uses ATP energy to push three positive sodium ions out of the cell.

5
00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:20.233 line:10%
Simultaneously it pulls two potassium ions in,

6
00:00:20.233 --> 00:00:24.079 line:10%
setting up the steep ion gradients across the membrane.

7
00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:29.191 line:10%
Then potassium leak channels allow those yellow ...

8
00:00:29.191 --> 00:00:33.525 line:10%
ions to diffuse back out, increasing the internal ...

9
00:00:33.525 --> 00:00:35.279 line:10%
negativity inside.

10
00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:38.585 line:10%
Massive negatively charged proteins stay trapped as they ...

11
00:00:38.585 --> 00:00:40.639 line:10%
are far too large to cross the barrier.

12
00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:42.521 line:10%
Together, these factors stabilize the ...

13
00:00:42.521 --> 00:00:45.599 line:10%
resting membrane potential at a steady negative 70 millivolts.

14
00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:49.040 line:10%
So why does the inside rest near minus 70 millivolts?

15
00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:51.758 line:10%
Potassium leaks outward down its gradient until the ...

16
00:00:51.758 --> 00:00:53.672 line:10%
negative interior almost pulls it back,

17
00:00:53.672 --> 00:00:56.319 line:10%
settling close to potassium's equilibrium potential.

18
00:00:56.560 --> 00:00:59.349 line:10%
And that charge is just a thin layer hugging the membrane ...

19
00:00:59.349 --> 00:01:00.239 line:10%
like a capacitor.

20
00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:03.800 line:10%
In short, three forces hold the cell ...

21
00:01:03.800 --> 00:01:05.360 line:10%
near -70 millivolts.

22
00:01:05.360 --> 00:01:07.840 line:10%
The sodium potassium pump builds the gradients.

23
00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:10.170 line:10%
Potassium then leaks outward through leak ...

24
00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:12.068 line:10%
channels, and large negatively charged ...

25
00:01:12.068 --> 00:01:13.519 line:10%
